# Minimal Tor configuration for the web_server onion service.
#
# This daemon exists to publish one v3 hidden service and nothing else: no SOCKS relay a client
# could use, no exit traffic, no directory mirror. It forwards the onion's virtual port 80 to the
# web container's :8000 over the compose network, so the address a visitor opens is the .onion and
# the app itself is never exposed to the host or the internet.
#
# The HiddenServiceDir holds the service's private key and its hostname file. It is a named volume
# in onion.yaml so the .onion survives a restart; that key is what *is* the address, so it is never
# committed and never baked into an image. See this directory's README for reading the hostname and
# for pinning a persistent or vanity key.

SocksPort 0
Log notice stderr

HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/hidden_service
HiddenServiceVersion 3
HiddenServicePort 80 web:8000

# The abuse brake: an onion service has no client IP to limit, so a client pays a proof of work to
# introduce itself once the queue is under pressure. Needs tor 0.4.8 or later built with --enable-gpl.
HiddenServicePoWDefensesEnabled 1
